From 40c2dd935fbe08b7cd4977f316ad690399500cdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:28:56 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: allow the highest numbered port to be
 allocated

Master port numbers start at 1, so the valid ports are 1..nports. The
pconfig array is sized and filled accordingly, but
qcom_swrm_stream_alloc_ports() rejects any port number >= nports, which
makes the last port unusable.

On SM8550 the TX master has four data ports and the WCD938x DMIC4-7
slave port is mapped to master port 4 through qcom,tx-port-mapping.
Capturing from one of those microphones then fails in hw_params with
"All ports busy".

Search and check against nports + 1 so that the last port can be used.

Signed-off-by: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 55678a30cd4a1e..f90817496b29d2 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1272,7 +1272,8 @@ static int qcom_swrm_stream_alloc_ports(struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl,
 			continue;
 
 		port_mask = &ctrl->port_mask;
-		maxport = ctrl->nports;
+		/* Port numbers start from 1, so the last valid one is nports */
+		maxport = ctrl->nports + 1;
 
 		list_for_each_entry(s_rt, &m_rt->slave_rt_list, m_rt_node) {
 			slave = s_rt->slave;
